.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt NEWFS_MSDOS 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm newfs_msdos
.Nd construct a new FAT file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl N
.Op Fl @ Ar offset
.Op Fl C Ar create-size
.Op Fl F Ar FAT-type
.Op Fl I Ar VolumeID
.Op Fl L Ar label
.Op Fl S Ar sector-size
.Op Fl T Ar timestamp
.Op Fl b Ar block-size
.Op Fl c Ar cluster-size
.Op Fl e Ar DirEnts
.Op Fl m Ar media
.Op Fl n Ar FATs
.Op Fl o Ar hidden
.Op Fl r Ar reserved
.Op Fl s Ar total
.Ar special
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
makes an empty FAT12, FAT16 or FAT32 file system on
.Ar special ,
a disk device or a file, for
.Xr mount_msdosfs 8 .
What isn't given is chosen from the size, by Microsoft's tables: the FAT type
(FAT12 under 16 MB, FAT16 under 512 MB, FAT32 above), the cluster size, the
root directory's size (FAT12 and FAT16) and the reserved sectors.
.Pp
Sizes may end in
.Cm k ,
.Cm m
or
.Cm g
(bytes) or
.Cm s
(sectors).
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl N
Show the layout; write nothing.
.It Fl @ Ar offset
Start the file system
.Ar offset
bytes into
.Ar special .
.It Fl C Ar create-size
Create
.Ar special
as a file of this size first (or grow it to it).
.It Fl F Ar FAT-type
12, 16 or 32.
.It Fl I Ar VolumeID
The volume's serial number; by default one derived from the time.
.It Fl L Ar label
The volume label, also written to the root directory.
.It Fl S Ar sector-size
Bytes per sector, a power of two from 512 to 4096; 512 by default.
.It Fl T Ar timestamp
Seconds since the epoch to derive the serial number and stamp the label from,
for repeatable images.
.It Fl b Ar block-size
Bytes per cluster.
.It Fl c Ar cluster-size
Sectors per cluster, a power of two.
.It Fl e Ar DirEnts
Root directory entries (FAT12 and FAT16).
.It Fl m Ar media
The media descriptor: 0xf0, or 0xf8 to 0xff; 0xf8 by default.
.It Fl n Ar FATs
Copies of the FAT; 2 by default.
.It Fl o Ar hidden
Hidden sectors, the partition's start, recorded in the boot sector.
.It Fl r Ar reserved
Reserved sectors.
.It Fl s Ar total
Use only
.Ar total
sectors of
.Ar special .
.El
.Pp
FAT32's FSInfo sector is sector 1 and its backup boot sector sector 6.
The boot sector holds no boot code.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
A FAT32 EFI system partition:
.Dl newfs_msdos -F 32 -L EFISYS /dev/gpt/efi
.Pp
A 1.44 MB floppy image:
.Dl newfs_msdos -C 1440k floppy.img
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr msdosfs 5 ,
.Xr fsck_msdosfs 8 ,
.Xr makefs 8 ,
.Xr mount_msdosfs 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
command appeared in
.Fx 3.0 .
.Sh BUGS
.Fx Ns 's
.Fl A ,
.Fl B ,
.Fl O ,
.Fl a ,
.Fl f ,
.Fl h ,
.Fl i ,
.Fl k
and
.Fl u
are not supported.
